Z||000000||banditbalz||05-21-2001||12:55 PM||||Grinthock and I are considering brake upgrades as we both need new REAR brakes.  His 87GT is not a daily driver so if it sits for a week while we do this it isn't an issue, what we are looking for are brake upgrades, larger rotors or better calipers and pads.<P>What has everyone here done?  What could we do that does not require much custom fabrication (we live in an apt building and don't have the space to do custom fab)?<P>Any ideas are great, details is good too.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Slammed Fiero||05-21-2001||01:04 PM||||I believe most major brake upgrades such as increase in size require hubs for the front. The grand am brake upgrade is popular and would be the best bet for both of you since you each have 15" wheels.  Anything such as a 11.25" brake upgrade will require the use of 16" or bigger wheels.<P>Take a look at <BR> <A HREF="http://www.ipass.net/~fieroman/terranexus/fieroman/walt/walt.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ipass.net/~fieroman/terranexus/fieroman/walt/walt.htm</A> <P>This is basically the conversion I did. The main page also has info on the GA setup.<P>Now I thought Grinthock was selling his Fiero?? <P><BR>P.S had a good night last night with you guys becky and Carrie , we should do it more often<BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||05-21-2001||01:23 PM||||Hey Grinthock and Banditbalz<BR>If you's are interested in driving a fiero with the Grand Am/Beretta upgrade in your area, come out to the Grand Bend meet June 9th @ 1.00, or 11:00 am in london. (see the thread re unofficial meet in Grand Bend) and you can test drive my wife's 86 GT with the conversion. or contact me re emails about what was done and cdn $$$||||reg||1
Z||000003||banditbalz||05-21-2001||01:49 PM||||While looking around the 'net we found this<BR> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-grandambrakes.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~nife/articles/tt-grandambrakes.html</A> <P>This guy says that the grandam parts just bolt right on!  True?<P><BR>After that altercation with the Navigator in Wasaga I do'nt really feel like nailing some loser because my back brakes suck (almost got him)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||PBJ||05-21-2001||03:43 PM||||try this <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/info.html</A> <P>a great place for ideas and success stories.  Has the brake upgrade in it.  Beretta and G/am are the same thing.  <BR>||||reg||1
