Z||000013||Oreif||05-22-2001||11:15 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B> Lisa;<P>   Why do you write messages like that and degrade your personality..... I will reiterate something I mentioned in another section regarding one of your posts.... Grow Up.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>grithock,<BR>It's obvious that the message from Lisa to Jonathan was an "inside joke". I think you need to "grow up" and not take everything typed in a post as a personal message to you.<BR>I have read the other posts and you need to "chill out" a little. Maybe you need some valium?<P>As for Archie's "big brake kit" I have been in 3 different cars that have had Archie's kit installed. The only thing I can say is it'll stop on a dime, pick it up, and give 2 nickle's for change! Rmember, with any "Big brake kit" you need 16" wheels (or larger).<BR>The 3-4 kits I have seen for sale (including Archie's) won't fit with the stock 15" wheels. <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">     <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||grinthock||05-22-2001||11:32 AM||||Thanks Oreif;<P>I AM getting some 16" wheels, so that's not an issue, but what I am saying is, I have been told that the grand Am FRONT mount calipers can go on the back with no problems, bolt right up... So if that's true, what calipers do I use with archies kit?<P>Not to slam the price (I will probably get BURNED for sayin this!) but I didn't want this to turn into a super mega expensive project but at $260 USD is a fair bit for me to spend (that's like $500 Canadian by the time I Get them here and that's just the adaptors!)<P>I understand that the performance will be amazing BUT, do I REALLY need to go this far?  Again, what kind of calipers does this kit use||||reg||1
Z||000015||Archie||05-22-2001||11:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>Ok, those 4 adaptors are to put on different calipers right?  What type are they?  Explain!! We need details here!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>To retain the handbrake you will use 2 Camaro calipers and 2 Caddie calipers (as pictured above). The Caddie calipers are pretty expensive, so if you don't need the h-brake, you can use Camaro calipers all around.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000016||Archie||05-22-2001||11:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>Thanks Oreif;<P>BUT, do I REALLY need to go this far?  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> joke follows  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>You may not want to go too far, we've already seen the results when you go too far.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000017||grinthock||05-22-2001||12:08 PM||||Touche Arch!<P>Nicely done!  <P>I am looking forward to meeting you personally at Michigan (I will be the guy with the belaclava on hiding from everyone!) <P>What fun the last 12 hours have been!<P><BR>It's a nice kit Archie, but I think it's a little too rich for my budget!  <P>Could I just get 2 of them from you and do JUST the back ? (That's where 90% of my problems are)||||reg||1
Z||000018||Yellow88GT||05-22-2001||12:33 PM||||Archie,<P>That kit is for an 84 thru 87, right?<BR>Do you have a kit for an 88, <BR>or is there another way I can upgrade to<BR>larger brakes.<P>I am running 17" rims and my little rotors <BR>look stupid  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thanks,<P>Jerry||||reg||1
Z||000019||Oreif||05-22-2001||02:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>Could I just get 2 of them from you and do JUST the back ? (That's where 90% of my problems are)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I think you should read Ogre's brake upgrade stuff in the cave. Using different calipers (even the Grand Am's) messes up the braking system. The proportioning valve and amount of pressure varies. (That is why Archie's kit has a different master cylinder) I don't think you'll be able to just do the rears and have the system work correctly.<P>As for cost, Going to bigger brakes is expensive. Archie's is the least. I have seen others for over $1500.00. I've even seen one that was just for the fronts and costs over $2500!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||grinthock||05-22-2001||07:24 PM||||What other upgrades have people here done to their brakes?  I hear all these things I can do, what's practical?  What's been done?||||reg||1
