Z||000022||KRMFiero||05-23-2001||07:27 AM||||Archie,<BR>What kind of Caddy calipers? would the ones of my 88 Seville 4 dr work? (Just wondering if i should pull before it goes back to the junk yard)<BR>also does the caddy calipers get used also for regular stoping? i would not really want it if it was only for the E-Brake. is there a way to hook it up to work WITH the camaro calipers?<P>Kyle<p>[This message has been edited by KRMFiero (edited 05-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||Archie||05-23-2001||07:47 AM||||The caddie calipers are from the rear of a 1980-1985 Seville.<P>Yeah, the rear brakes work as regular brakes too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Like I said before, you can use the inexpensive Camaro Calipers on all 4 wheels but you will not have the H-Brake.<P>Archie ||||reg||1
